  "message_type": "WRFC_INVOKE_RESPONSE",
  "capture_source": "live capture 2026-09-03; SAP A4H kernel 793. Successful STFC_CONNECTION reply over WebSocket RFC. Sanitised: the RESPTEXT value, which reports the system id, date, time and logon data, is replaced with a same-width string so every offset and length stays valid.",
  "evidence": "parse_invoke_response reads it without modification, returning ECHOTEXT='probe' -- the value sent in wrfc_invoke_request.bin",
  "expected_parse": {
    "ECHOTEXT": "probe",
    "return_code": 0,
    "raises": null
  },
  "notes": [
    "A wRFC response is a classic response TLV stream without the GW header, so the classic parser reads it. That is the counterpart to the request finding: neither direction needed a wRFC-specific codec.",
    "0x0503 present and 0x0417 absent with 0x0420 zero is the success shape documented in framing.md.",
    "0x0514 echoes the session token the client proposed in its LOGON."
  ],
